  "limits": [
    "Shared-DAG binding construction improves; generic type/physical/logical lowering still expands deep shared graphs. Both depth16 actions hit20-second caps. No action-speedup or linear total-construction/compilation claim.",
    "Categorical validation and total are shared for scalar weights; selection deliberately remains the original linear subtractive scan for seeded floating-point compatibility. Per-row weights require per-row validation.",
    "Nondegenerate hypergeometric sampling retains sample-count work to preserve seeded streams. Only isolated direct or all-remaining-deterministic outcomes skip draws.",
    "Callback indexing retains underlying value buffers and constructs visible-window ordinal/offset buffers. Final downstream casts may canonicalize alternate string storage.",
    "Random list/ndarray outputs still have per-owning-row Arrow containers; element payloads use typed buffers and shuffle uses one batched Arrow take.",
    "Dirichlet preserves ordinary raw values/draws. Overflow and all-underflow use same-draw normalization fallbacks; empty/all-zero vectors are invalid.",
    "One known patched Vortex nested-list writer test was excluded per user instruction; no dependency code reviewed or changed."
  ]
